        <bpmn:outgoing>W3582_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3582_Task5" name="Enterprise Architects (Infra) maintain the infrastructure reference…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Enterprise Architects (Infra) maintain the infrastructure reference architecture and standards: high-availability/DR patterns (links to VS-26/W3590), performance/scale targets (model-company §15.3), observability/monitoring (links to VS-27.1), automation/infrastructure-as-code, and the approved services list (links to W3572); align to security (W3583)
Responsible (R): Enterprise Architects (Infra) / IT Ops
Accountable (A): Chief Enterprise Architect
Duration: Maintained</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3582_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3582_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3582_Task6" name="Enterprise Architects (Infra)/IT Operations review each workload&#x27;s…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Enterprise Architects (Infra)/IT Operations review each workload&#x27;s infrastructure design via the ARB (W3571/W3580): sizing, HA/DR, cost (links to W3588), security (links to W3583), and operational supportability (links to VS-27.1); manage capacity, cost optimization, and FinOps (links to VS-99.3)
Responsible (R): Enterprise Architects (Infra) / IT Ops
Accountable (A): Chief Enterprise Architect
Duration: Per workload + continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3582_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3582_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
