      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3583_Task4" name="Enterprise Architects (Security)/IT Security Manager define the security…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Enterprise Architects (Security)/IT Security Manager define the security architecture and strategy: zero-trust model, identity &amp; access management (links to VS-27.3), network/segmentation, encryption (data-in-transit/rest), secrets/key management, application security, API security (W3579), and security operations/SIEM (links to VS-27.3); align to the security program and regulatory obligations (links to VS-91/VS-86)
Responsible (R): Enterprise Architects (Security) / IT Security Manager
Accountable (A): Chief Enterprise Architect
Duration: Strategy + maintained</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3583_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3583_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3583_Task5" name="Enterprise Architects (Security) maintain the security reference architecture…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Enterprise Architects (Security) maintain the security reference architecture and standards: secure-by-design patterns, authentication/authorization standards, data-classification handling (links to VS-91), logging/audit (links to VS-27.3/VS-88), and the security control catalog mapping to frameworks (links to VS-27.3); enforce via ARB (W3571)
Responsible (R): Enterprise Architects (Security) / IT Security Manager
Accountable (A): Chief Enterprise Architect
Duration: Maintained</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3583_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3583_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3583_Task6" name="Enterprise Architects (Security)/IT Security Manager review each initiative&#x27;s…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Enterprise Architects (Security)/IT Security Manager review each initiative&#x27;s security design via the ARB (W3571/W3580): threat model, controls, privacy (links to VS-91), third-party/vendor security (links to VS-03/VS-99), and residual risk; integrate to the cybersecurity program (links to VS-27.3) and audit (links to VS-21)
Responsible (R): Enterprise Architects (Security) / IT Security Manager
Accountable (A): Chief Enterprise Architect
Duration: Per initiative</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3583_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3583_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
