    <bpmn:process id="W_W3584" name="W3584. Architecture for ERP Platform &amp; Core Systems Evolution" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: ERP/core-systems roadmap (W3585); release/upgrade cycle; capability gap
Frequency: Per release/upgrade + roadmap cycle
Volume: Core ERP + surrounding core systems (POS, WMS, ecommerce, MDM, loyalty, payments)
Owner: Enterprise Architects
Participants: Enterprise Architects, ERP/Core-Systems Owners, IT Operations (links to VS-27), PMO (links to VS-112), Innovation (links to VS-30), Vendor Mgmt (links to VS-03/VS-34), Business Capability Owners
Source: workflow W3584 — Architecture for ERP Platform &amp; Core Systems Evolution</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3584_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3584_Lane1" name="Enterprise Architects">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3584_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3584_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3584_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3584_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3584_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3584_Start3" name="ERP/core-systems roadmap (W3585); release/upgrade cycle; capability gap">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3584_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W3584_Task4" name="Enterprise Architects/Core-Systems Owners define the ERP and core-systems…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Enterprise Architects/Core-Systems Owners define the ERP and core-systems evolution architecture: ERP-centric reference architecture (W3570), extension vs. customization policy (prefer configured/standard over custom), the surrounding application estate (POS links to VS-08, WMS links to VS-04, ecommerce links to VS-10, MDM links to VS-29, loyalty links to VS-13, payments links to VS-80), and the upgrade/release strategy
Responsible (R): Enterprise Architects / Core-Systems Owners
Accountable (A): Chief Enterprise Architect
Duration: Strategy + per release</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3584_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3584_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W3584_Task5" name="Enterprise Architects govern ERP releases/upgrades: scope (new capability vs…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Enterprise Architects govern ERP releases/upgrades: scope (new capability vs. technical/refresh), regression/integration impact (W3579), data migration (W3581/links to data-migration-mapping), cutover/rollout (links to VS-27.1/VS-112), rollback, and the customization-debt impact (W3578); route significant changes through the ARB (W3571)
Responsible (R): Enterprise Architects / Core-Systems Owners
Accountable (A): Chief Enterprise Architect
Duration: Per release</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3584_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3584_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3584_Task6" name="Enterprise Architects manage the core-systems capability roadmap: when a…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Enterprise Architects manage the core-systems capability roadmap: when a capability runs in-suite vs. as a built platform, retirement of redundant surrounding applications (W3578), and alignment to the technology roadmap (W3585) and business capabilities (links to VS-33); report core-systems health and evolution to governance (W3592)
Responsible (R): Enterprise Architects
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Roadmap cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3584_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3584_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3584_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3584_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3584_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-569 (ensure controlled execution — Application Portfolio, Integration &amp; Solution Architecture (PA-113.2).) | - operational: extension-vs-customization policy; operational: regression/integration testing and staged rollout
Owner: Enterprise Architects</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
