    <bpmn:process id="W_W5516" name="W5516. Best-of-Breed Product Lifecycle Management, Vendor Release Intake &amp; Exit Reserves" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Vendor release notification; contract signature/renewal; annual TPRM reassessment; QBR cycle; vendor health/EOL signal
Frequency: Per vendor release + monthly product health + quarterly/annual lifecycle cycles
Volume: ~9 vendor-managed products (vendor commodities incl. foundation-model API contracts, the already-built POS/ecommerce/loyalty platforms, and the in-suite EBS currency program) × ~6–12 vendor releases/product/year ≈ 54–108 release intakes/year; carried by 4 Vendor PM seats (WLI ×2, SSP ×1, CCP ×1) plus the CIO Office secretariat
Owner: Vendor Product Manager (owning domain team, per managed product)
Participants: Vendor Product Managers (WLI ×2, SSP ×1, CCP ×1), CIO Office vendor-portfolio analyst (Register &amp; exit-reserve records), domain QA &amp; release analysts (regression pack), SEC TPRM analyst (links to VS-161), IAP (contract catalog &amp; consumer tests — links to W3579), INFRA (staging rings), Procurement/Legal (links to VS-34/VS-100.3), Tier &amp; Control Board (escalation), application lifecycle owner (links to W3578)
Source: workflow W5516 — Best-of-Breed Product Lifecycle Management, Vendor Release Intake &amp; Exit Reserves</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5516_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5516_Lane1" name="Vendor PM">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5516_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5516_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5516_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5516_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5516_Lane2" name="Procurement">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5516_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5516_Lane3" name="SEC TPRM analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5516_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5516_Lane4" name="Vendor-portfolio analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5516_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5516_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5516_Start6" name="Vendor release notification; contract signature/renewal; annual TPRM reassessment; QBR…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5516_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5516_Task7" name="Vendor Product Manager run release intake: vendor releases land in the owning…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Vendor Product Manager run release intake: vendor releases land in the owning team&#x27;s staging ring and pass the intake checklist plus the domain regression pack (Tier-1 workflow coverage mandatory) before production — the same standard the in-suite EBS currency (RUP/CPU) cycle meets; a release may be deferred one cycle, never two
Responsible (R): Vendor PM / QA &amp; release analyst
Accountable (A): Owning team IT PO
Duration: 4–8 hours/release</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5516_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5516_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5516_Task8" name="Vendor PM/IT PO track the upgrade-currency KPI — at most one major version…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Vendor PM/IT PO track the upgrade-currency KPI — at most one major version behind vendor current per product; a product two versions behind is a Tier &amp; Control Board escalation with a funded remediation plan
Responsible (R): Vendor PM
Accountable (A): Owning team IT PO
Duration: Monthly check</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5516_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5516_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5516_Task9" name="Procurement/Legal/Vendor PM verify the required contract clauses at signature…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Procurement/Legal/Vendor PM verify the required contract clauses at signature and each renewal: Philippine data-residency/processing terms (RA 10173), statutory-readiness warranty where applicable, exit/transition assistance, data-export in open formats, and price-escalation caps
Responsible (R): Procurement / Legal / Vendor PM
Accountable (A): Owning team IT PO
Duration: Per signature/renewal</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5516_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5516_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5516_Task10" name="SEC/TPRM keep every managed vendor risk-tiered with tier-1 annual reassessment…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: SEC/TPRM keep every managed vendor risk-tiered with tier-1 annual reassessment and audit-report review (links to VS-161/W4729); continuous-monitoring feeds (financial, cyber, performance) watch vendor health and EOL (links to W4734)
Responsible (R): SEC TPRM analyst
Accountable (A): SEC lead
Duration: Annual + continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5516_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5516_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5516_Task11" name="CIO Office accrue each replaceable vendor dependency&#x27;s exit reserve at every…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: CIO Office accrue each replaceable vendor dependency&#x27;s exit reserve at every QBR (a set percentage of license cost, held centrally) and disclose reserves in the QBR FinOps pack — a vendor exit is never unfundable; the in-house platforms are forever by doctrine, so their resilience is a DR/run-cost question, not an exit question (links to VS-135)
Responsible (R): Vendor-portfolio analyst / FinOps
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5516_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5516_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5516_Task12" name="Vendor PM/CIO Office manage product health: SLA attainment, integration latency…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Vendor PM/CIO Office manage product health: SLA attainment, integration latency vs IAP budget, roadmap intelligence, and the Register&#x27;s re-evaluation triggers (links to W5515); sunset decisions route through W3578 application retirement and the SIB (W5515)
Responsible (R): Vendor PM / Vendor-portfolio analyst
Accountable (A): Owning team IT PO
Duration: Monthly + per trigger</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5516_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5516_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5516_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5516_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5516_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-569 (ensure controlled execution — Application Portfolio, Integration &amp; Solution Architecture (PA-113.2).) | - operational: vendor releases pass the domain regression pack (Tier-1 mandatory) before production | - operational: upgrade-currency KPI — defer one cycle, never two; Tier &amp; Control Board escalation at two behind | - operational: exit reserve accrued at every QBR; contract clauses (data residency, exit assistance, export, price caps) verified at signature and renewal
Owner: Vendor Product Manager (owning domain team, per managed product)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5516_Assoc15" sourceRef="W5516_Annotation14" targetRef="W5516_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
