    <bpmn:process id="W_W5535" name="W5535. Capability Demand Intake &amp; Backlog Triage" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: A BPO or executive stakeholder raises a new software-capability need with their paired IT PO/PM; a quarterly roadmap re-plan; an annual QBR structural review; or a fired sourcing re-evaluation trigger needing re-triage (links to W5515)
Frequency: Continuous intake; quarterly roadmap re-plan; annual QBR structural review
Volume: One front door for the whole 17-product estate — ~40–60 new-capability items/year reach EA triage (routine enhancements resolve in team backlogs at the weekly BPO–PO refinement and never escalate); each quarterly re-plan re-triages 4–8 carried-over items
Owner: Head of Enterprise Architecture
Participants: Head of EA, owning team IT PO/PM &amp; BPO (the stakeholder&#x27;s single face), product/process architects, CIO (Product Council chair), FinOps/TBM analyst (links to VS-135), vendor-portfolio analyst, ARB (links to W3571), SEC privacy/TPRM pre-read for customer-data surfaces (links to VS-161), PMO for initiative-sized routing (links to VS-112)
Source: workflow W5535 — Capability Demand Intake &amp; Backlog Triage</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5535_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5535_Lane1" name="Owning PO &amp; BPO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5535_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5535_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5535_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5535_Lane2" name="Head of EA">
