      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5535_Start6" name="A BPO or executive stakeholder raises a new software-capability need with their paired IT…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5535_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5535_Task7" name="Log the raised need in the owning product&#x27;s backlog and classify it against the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Log the raised need in the owning product&#x27;s backlog and classify it against the 188-VS catalog: (a) enhancement of an existing product → stays in the team backlog; (b) a missing workflow-level owner inside an existing value stream → owning team + architect for gap-admission; (c) a genuinely new capability or value stream → sourcing-candidate triage (Step 3)
Responsible (R): Owning PO &amp; BPO / Head of EA
Accountable (A): Head of EA
Duration: 2–6 hours/item</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5535_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5535_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5535_Task8" name="Close the loop with the stakeholder through the BPO: every logged item carries…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Close the loop with the stakeholder through the BPO: every logged item carries an accepted / routed / declined-with-reason state — a stakeholder never waits on an unacknowledged request
Responsible (R): Owning PO &amp; BPO
Accountable (A): Owning team IT PO
Duration: 1 hour/item</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5535_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5535_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5535_Task9" name="For sourcing candidates, assemble the triage pack: BPO outcome statement &amp;…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: For sourcing candidates, assemble the triage pack: BPO outcome statement &amp; KPIs, the architect&#x27;s integration sketch over the IAP contract patterns (links to W3579), a rough TCO (links to W4100), compliance constraints (RA 10173 privacy for customer data; BIR official receipts for billed services), and a preliminary Tier proposal
Responsible (R): Head of EA / FinOps
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 4–12 hours/candidate</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5535_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5535_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5535_Task10" name="Route the outcome: backlog items → owning-PO prioritization via the roadmap…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Route the outcome: backlog items → owning-PO prioritization via the roadmap; new-workflow/VS admissions → the workflow-catalog gap-analysis path; new capabilities → a sourcing proposal to the SIB gate (links to W5515); initiative-sized delivery → the PMO (links to VS-112)
Responsible (R): Head of EA
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Per item</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5535_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5535_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5535_Task11" name="Fund and schedule accepted items at the Product Council — capacity is allocated…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Fund and schedule accepted items at the Product Council — capacity is allocated as funding runs, not projects; roadmap approval above PHP 5M; the quarterly re-plan sequences winners into release trains and rings
Responsible (R): Domain PO
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: At monthly Product Council</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5535_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5535_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5535_Task12" name="Keep the intake register state current — accepted/routed/declined outcomes feed…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Keep the intake register state current — accepted/routed/declined outcomes feed portfolio reporting (links to W3592) and the QBR outcome review; declined items return to the stakeholder with the rationale via the BPO
Responsible (R): Vendor-portfolio analyst
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Quarterly + continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5535_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5535_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5535_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5535_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5535_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-569 (ensure controlled execution — Application Portfolio, Integration &amp; Solution Architecture (PA-113.2).) | - operational: every new-capability request carries an accepted/routed/declined state before any procurement or build begins | - operational: sourcing candidates route only through the SIB gate (W5515); no tooling is procured directly from an intake item
Owner: Head of Enterprise Architecture</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5535_Assoc15" sourceRef="W5535_Annotation14" targetRef="W5535_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
